# Nivo78 Rule Projection — 02-ui-input-save

**Binding status:** This file is a maintained enforcement projection of the canonical Nivo78 Product Standard.
**Source:** `reference/NIVO78_APP_STANDARD.txt`
**Authority:** The canonical standard and rule-ID catalog control if this projection and the source ever differ.

## Agent instructions
- Apply this rule whenever the work described by the rule is relevant.
- Treat every requirement below as binding unless the canonical standard marks it as `[QA]`/conditional or an approved override applies.
- Preserve and mention canonical `APP-*`, `WEB-*`, `MARKETING-*`, and other rule IDs when reporting compliance or exceptions.
- Do not weaken a requirement merely because it is inconvenient to implement.
- If a requirement cannot be met, stop before shipping and use the standard override process.

---

Technical bar for a good Nivo78 app (engineering — not
customer marketing)

\- Shared outlined fields on critical paths; engine
validation; Enter/IME and blur commit (APP-INPUT-COMMIT).

\- Required format/validate on blur / Done / leave /
Save only (APP-INPUT-FORMAT-ON-COMMIT).

\- Flush blur-only drafts before same-screen persist
(Save / Lock / Next / Finish) and before

  page-leave
persist — a control that does not steal focus still writes what is on screen

 
(APP-INPUT-FLUSH-BEFORE-PERSIST). Persist from the inner field commit
(the text just typed).

  Do not persist
a leftover parent copy, and do not persist a leftover composed snapshot of the

  form after
that flush.

\- Save is inactive when the on-screen draft matches
the last registry-verified values; active

  when dirty;
inactive again only after flush + write + read-back
(APP-SAVE-VERIFIED-INACTIVE).

  Confirmation
is inactive Save, not a success toast. Failed write keeps Save active.

\- Home / Back from a typed Save page: when the draft
differs from last verified values,

  flush and
persist when engine validation passes, then leave (APP-LEAVE-DIRTY-PROMPT).

  Invalid draft
or failed write blocks leave with field errors or failure toast. Say on the

  page: Valid
changes save when you leave. Instant controls (toggles, chips) MAY persist

  immediately.
Optional Save / Don't save / Stay dialog only with accepted override.

\- Focus places caret for in-place edit — never select-all
or clear on focus (APP-INPUT-FOCUS-EDIT-ONLY).

\- Minimum 44×44 dp touch targets on mobile; contrast
and Dynamic Type / Large Text (APP-UI-A11Y-FLOOR).

\- Universal UI, HiDPI Resolution, and Display Scaling Awareness: Every application MUST be
display resolution aware and fully operational on high-resolution displays (HiDPI / 4K / Retina).
Apps must be fully scalable across all screen zoom levels, display DPI scaling (100% to
300%+), and per-monitor dynamic DPI transitions. Desktop apps must configure per-monitor
high-DPI mode at startup before font or UI creation. No fixed 96-DPI pixel constraints
on input heights, button dimensions, sliders, spinners, or container bounds. Every control,
text string, icon, glyph, and dialog must scale dynamically with font metrics and DPI factors
without blurriness, clipping, squashing, overlapping, or text truncation (APP-A11Y-TEXT-SCALING).

\- No silent remount or sibling-field wipe while the
operator is editing related rows (e.g. profile revision

  bumps that
discard in-progress drafts on the same screen).

\- Dirty / required / Save UI must not lie while the
user is typing — use live draft when storage commits on blur.

\- One shared field component family on critical form
paths — no one-off Material fields that drift from the standard.

\- These rules are build/QA requirements. Do not put
them in Brand Philosophy, About, store, or product will/won’t marketing copy.

\- Debug-only breadcrumb troubleshooting (engineering —
not customer marketing): every Nivo78 app

  MUST keep a
10,000-event local ring buffer in DEBUG builds (UI events, function calls,
navigation,

  text-input
\*length\* only). Release builds MUST no-op \`log()\` on the first line (\`if
(!isDebugBuild)

  return\`) with
zero ring-buffer allocation. The file export \`attachBreadcrumbsToBugReport\`
MUST live

  only in
\`src/debug\` / \`src/androidDebug\` — never main, androidMain, or release. MUST
NOT log raw

  field text,
secrets, or PII. MUST NOT appear in store listings or customer will/won’t copy.



What a good Nivo78 app will do

\- Present the right data at the right step — field,
screen, and time aligned to the user’s job.

\- Guided checklists someone can finish without
memorizing external manuals.

\- Let the operator finish a real task in one sitting —
no “come back later” traps (forced tours, account gates,

  or walls that
demand unrelated fields). Optional facts (e.g. full address) stay optional
until the job needs them.

\- Use honest defaults for a real solo day — empty or
zero where empty is true; not demo theater or fake sample data.

\- Make Cancel, Discard, Decline, and Exit match their
labels — the safe choice is always the labeled safe choice.

\- Edit-until-handoff; validate before save, not only
at export.

\- Persist what is on the screen when the user taps
Save, Lock, Next, or Finish — including a

  field that is
still focused. The operator does not have to tap away first. Reopen the record

  and see the
same values that were on screen (duration, line items, settings rows).

\- Keep Save inactive until the draft differs from the
last registry-verified values; after Save,

  keep it active
until a read-back confirms those values are stored, then make it inactive

 
(APP-SAVE-VERIFIED-INACTIVE).

\- On Home or Back with typed changes next to Save: valid
drafts persist on leave; invalid or

  failed save
blocks leave (APP-LEAVE-DIRTY-PROMPT). Valid changes save when you leave.

\- If the OS kills the process while backgrounded, the
next cold start resumes the exact screen

  and draft —
not a false empty workspace (APP-LIFECYCLE-STATE-RESTORE).

\- Core business data exportable in an openly readable
standard (SQLite, JSON, CSV) without the

  app shell or a
proprietary service (APP-DATA-OPEN-EXPORT).

\- Keep Help, website will/won’t (or equivalent
limits), and the screen in agreement — if they disagree, the product is wrong.

\- Fail closed with a plain next step (corrupt file,
bad restore, unsupported schema) — never a blank workspace that looks empty.

\- On handoffs, state what the app produced, what the
user still does externally, and what was not sent

  (did not email
the client, did not upload, did not charge) unless that action truly shipped.

\- Keep screens dense but scannable in a few seconds:
title → status → next action.

\- Prepare and check; the user owns the last mile
(portal, bank, calendar, mail app) unless the product

  explicitly
ships and labels that mile.

\- Scannable progress so gaps are obvious before
external handoff.

\- Collect once, reuse everywhere; portable exports
(PDF, CSV, encrypted backup, copy sheets).

\- Let the user leave with their data (export/backup)
without calling support.

\- Fully offline everyday work; optional online
features user-initiated and labeled.

\- Remain useful for years offline even if a cloud
side-project ends.

\- ? help on non-trivial fields + searchable Help hub +
nivo78.com support articles.

\- Native handoffs for send (email, SMS, calendar,
browser) — user confirms send; app never silently transmits.

\- Honest free tiers with real limits, not demo timers.

\- Look and operate like other Nivo78 apps — shared
theme, menu contract, input/output patterns

  (learn one
app, know the chrome of the next: Help → Feedback → Support center → Privacy →
Terms → Check for updates → About, save bar, ? help).

\- Phone, tablet, and desktop may look different; business
rules and validation stay the same.

\- Family utilities (the /tools/ catalog: Estimate,
Measure, and the rest) are designed to run on

  Windows, Mac,
Android phones and tablets, iPhone, and iPad. One business-rules engine. Do not

  stamp a new
utility as phone-only or Windows-only unless the job itself requires it (APA:

  store listing
prep on a Windows PC) and an accepted override records that exception.

  Website and
Help MUST say Not yet / in development until a public install exists — never
Yes

  without a
channel, and never No for a surface that is still in the family design.

\- Interruptions are rare; when they appear they are
consequential (legal gate, vault, overwrite) — not nags.

\- Embody Brand Philosophy: local-first, respectful,
transparent, fast/reliable, built to last.

\- Earn trust with honest scope — website and Help name
capabilities and limitations so there are

  no negative
surprises after install.

\- Issue a one-time recovery key when the master
password is created (and a new key after a

  recovery-key
reset). Tell the user to store it off the device and why. The key sets a new

  master
password; it does not reveal the old password. Nivo78 cannot recover either
secret.

\- In DEBUG builds only, keep a local 10,000-event
breadcrumb ring buffer (UI, navigation, function

  calls, input
length — never raw text) so in-app bug reports can attach a troubleshooting
file.

  Release builds
discard every event with zero ring-buffer allocation.



What a good Nivo78 app will not do

Access and money

\- No required host login (Nivo78 account or cloud
sign-in) for core offline work.

\- No nags, sponsored rows, or “watch this to continue.”

\- No tolls on using the app without valid maintenance,
development, or infrastructure costs. This is one of the ways we keep your
costs low.

\- No toll on finished offline work that does not need
our servers (open old projects, export, print,

  backup) merely
because a subscription lapsed — charge for ongoing support, updates, or real

 
infrastructure, not for opening the user’s own data.

\- No dark-pattern upgrade walls mid-task (“pay to save
what you already typed”).

\- No hidden pricing or surprise microtransactions.



Data and network

\- No background upload of the business database or
project folder.

\- No selling data, advertising profiles, or silent
behavioral tracking for resale.

\- No internet required merely to open or use the core
offline job.

\- No silent email, SMS, calendar, or payment sends.

\- No silent diagnostics collection or background bug
reporting.

\- No breadcrumb logger, UI-event ring buffer, or debug
breadcrumb export in any \*\*release\*\* build

  (debug-only
troubleshooting is mandatory; shipping it in release is a defect).



Trust and control

\- No silent or pre-checked legal acceptance.

\- No delete or overwrite without a clear confirm.

\- No false empty workspace after a failed load,
corrupt file, or unsupported schema.

\- No proprietary-only lock-in — exports and backups
stay portable.

\- No “AI will handle it” (or similar automation)
unless that capability is shipped and labeled

  in the current
build.

\- No stack traces or internal error codes on primary
user-facing rows.

\- No email, SMS, or support reset of the master
password. No Nivo78 account to recover it.

  A recovery key
the user stored off-device is the only emergency path to set a new master
password.



Attention and scope

\- No nag screens, review spam, or engagement feeds.

\- No second product inside the product (social, news,
unrelated tools).

\- No forced tours or account gates before a usable
first pass.

\- No walls that demand unrelated optional fields
before the operator can finish setup.

\- No jargon walls on primary form rows.

\- No decorative hero screens inside the core job.

\- No excessive permissions unrelated to the job.

\- No “everything platform” scope creep.



Honesty

\- No Help / website / in-app disagreement about the
same capability or limit.

\- No “coming soon,” “planned,” or roadmap language
sold as shipped.

\- No mislabelled Cancel, Discard, Decline, or Exit
that does not match what the button does.

\- No dishonest defaults or demo theater that pretends
real data was already entered.

\- No overselling features or burying material limits
so customers discover the gap only after

  they rely on
the product.

\- No persist of a stale stored value while a focused
field still holds a newer draft

  (operator must
not have to tap away before Save, Lock, Next, or Finish).

\- No persist of a leftover composed form snapshot that
drops what is on screen.



Pre-ship bar (minimum)

\- Engine and UI separation verified; no platform
leakage in shared logic.

\- User-facing strings scanned for jargon and honesty;
help updated for new fields and tasks —

  including
limits and handoffs that prevent negative surprises.

\- Shared profile fields not duplicated; validation
before save on critical paths.

\- Input focus is in-place edit only — no select-all or
clear on focus (APP-INPUT-FOCUS-EDIT-ONLY).

\- Save/Lock/Next/Finish persist inner committed text
and live form fields (APP-INPUT-FLUSH-BEFORE-PERSIST).

\- Save inactive vs verified registry values; persist
valid on leave, block invalid leave (APP-SAVE-VERIFIED-INACTIVE,
APP-LEAVE-DIRTY-PROMPT).

\- Accessibility floor on mobile: 44×44 dp targets,
contrast, Dynamic Type (APP-UI-A11Y-FLOOR).

\- No silent remount wiping sibling drafts;
dirty/required UI honest while typing (live draft when blur-commit).

\- Offline core path works; vault and secret rules
honored.

\- Destructive actions confirmed; load/migrate fail
closed; empty/error states on major screens.

\- Setup path finishes a usable first pass without
traps; optional fields stay optional; Cancel/Decline match labels.

\- Handoff screens state what was produced, what the
user still does, and what was not sent.

\- Engine tests and product regression verify green
before release.

\- Copy voice: plain, practical, respectful — written
for a person doing real work, not for a pitch deck.

\- Web and Help will/won’t (or equivalent limit
statements) match shipped behavior — trust test passed.

\- Public web pages: comprehensive SEO head
(description, canonical, Open Graph, Twitter) on every page touched; website
verify green including WEB SEO checks.

